DISTRICTS

00:43:01.850 --> 00:43:04.969
IN AREAS CATEGORIZED AS HIGH
OR VERY

00:43:04.969 --> 00:43:07.640
HIGH FIRE HAZARD SEVERITY ZONES.

00:43:07.640 --> 00:43:09.560
AND HOW THIS ALL CAME ABOUT.

00:43:09.620 --> 00:43:12.290
UM, HISTORICALLY, WE HAD TRIED
NUMEROUS

00:43:12.290 --> 00:43:14.390
TIMES TO GET A BUDGET
ALLOCATIONS

00:43:14.390 --> 00:43:16.760
TO HELP FUND HEAVY EQUIPMENT

00:43:16.760 --> 00:43:18.770
AND FIREFIGHTING EQUIPMENT,

00:43:18.830 --> 00:43:22.850
UM, IN BACK COUNTRY HIGH FIRE
RISK AREAS.

00:43:22.850 --> 00:43:26.330
AND WE FOUND A STUDY SEVERAL
YEARS AGO

00:43:26.330 --> 00:43:28.880
THAT SHOWS THAT IN SAN DIEGO
COUNTY.

00:43:28.880 --> 00:43:31.580
AND IT RELATES STATEWIDE AS
WELL.

00:43:31.580 --> 00:43:35.330
ALMOST 25% OF WILDFIRES IN THE
BACK COUNTRY ARE

00:43:35.330 --> 00:43:38.360
CAUSED BY VEHICLES PULLING OFF
THE ROADWAY.

00:43:38.360 --> 00:43:40.790
SO THE CONCERN IS TO MAKE SURE
WE'RE

00:43:40.790 --> 00:43:43.430
GETTING THOSE BACK COUNTRY
ROADS,

00:43:43.430 --> 00:43:45.980
UH, CLEARED OF VEGETATION ALONG
THE SIDE.

00:43:45.980 --> 00:43:48.230
AND THAT COULD CUT DOWN A
SUBSTANTIAL

00:43:48.230 --> 00:43:50.270
AMOUNT OF THE FIRES THAT WE ARE

00:43:50.270 --> 00:43:53.570
EXPERIENCING BY DIRECTING
RESOURCES

00:43:53.570 --> 00:43:55.790
TOWARDS THESE HIGH RISK AREAS.

00:43:56.000 --> 00:44:00.110
AB 1819 ENSURES THAT THE MOST
VULNERABLE COMMUNITIES

00:44:00.110 --> 00:44:03.140
ARE BETTER PROTECTED AGAINST
FUTURE WILDFIRES.

00:44:03.140 --> 00:44:05.930
THESE DISTRICTS WILL GENERATE
FUNDS SPECIFICALLY

00:44:05.930 --> 00:44:07.640
FOR WILDFIRE MITIGATION EFFORTS,

00:44:07.640 --> 00:44:10.640
SUCH AS HEAVY EQUIPMENT TO CLEAR
VEGETATION,

00:44:10.640 --> 00:44:13.640
CREATING FIRE BREAKS AND
HARDENING INFRASTRUCTURE.

00:44:13.850 --> 00:44:15.320
AS WE'VE SEEN IN RECENT YEARS,

00:44:15.320 --> 00:44:16.820
THE FREQUENCY AND INTENSITY

00:44:16.820 --> 00:44:18.170
OF WILDFIRES IN CALIFORNIA

00:44:18.170 --> 00:44:20.989
HAS POSED SIGNIFICANT RISKS TO
LIVES,

00:44:20.989 --> 00:44:23.120
PROPERTIES AND OUR ENVIRONMENT.

00:44:23.390 --> 00:44:26.180
LAST YEAR, OVER 7000 FIRES
BURNED

00:44:26.180 --> 00:44:28.760
CLOSE TO 325,000 ACRES.

00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:30.830
THIS IS A CLEAR SIGNAL THAT OUR
CURRENT

00:44:30.830 --> 00:44:32.810
EFFORTS MUST GO FURTHER.

00:44:32.810 --> 00:44:35.600
IN A TIME WHERE OUR BUDGET IS
IN A DEFICIT,

00:44:35.600 --> 00:44:38.180
CREATING A PROGRAM THAT DOES NOT
RAISE TAXES

00:44:38.180 --> 00:44:40.640
OR IMPACT THE STATE BUDGET MAKES
SENSE.

00:44:41.270 --> 00:44:44.030
PLEASE WELCOME FIRE CHIEF JOE
NAPIER FROM

00:44:44.030 --> 00:44:46.520
VALLEY CENTER FIRE PROTECTION
DISTRICT

00:44:46.760 --> 00:44:48.980
TO DISCUSS THE CRITICAL
IMPORTANCE OF

00:44:48.980 --> 00:44:51.920
AB 1819 FOR WILDFIRE MITIGATION.

00:44:52.550 --> 00:44:55.880
AND WE ALSO HAVE MARCUS DETWILER
WITH

00:44:55.880 --> 00:44:58.370
THE SPECIAL DISTRICTS
ASSOCIATION.

00:44:59.370 --> 00:45:00.870
WELCOME TO THE WITNESSES.

00:45:00.870 --> 00:45:04.739
AND IF YOU CAN KEEP IT FAIRLY
BRIEF,

00:45:04.739 --> 00:45:05.460
THAT WOULD BE AWESOME.

00:45:05.460 --> 00:45:06.810
WE HAVE A LONG AGENDA TODAY.

00:45:06.810 --> 00:45:07.350
THANK YOU.

00:45:07.350 --> 00:45:08.100
I'LL DO MY BEST, SIR.

00:45:08.100 --> 00:45:08.820
THANK YOU.

00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:10.320
UH, ASSEMBLY MEMBER WALDRON.

00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:12.000
AND TO THE CHAIR AND TO THE
COMMITTEE.

00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:14.910
THANK YOU FOR HAVING ME HERE
AGAIN, JOE NAPIER.

00:45:14.910 --> 00:45:15.930
I'M THE FIRE CHIEF OF THE VALLEY

00:45:15.930 --> 00:45:17.250
CENTER FIRE PROTECTION DISTRICT,

00:45:17.250 --> 00:45:19.410
WHICH IS AN 85 SQUARE MILE
SPECIAL

00:45:19.410 --> 00:45:20.370
DISTRICT AT THE BASE

00:45:20.370 --> 00:45:23.430
OF PALOMAR MOUNTAIN IN NORTH SAN
DIEGO COUNTY.

00:45:23.940 --> 00:45:26.760
AND I'M HERE TO SUPPORT AB 1819,

00:45:26.760 --> 00:45:27.930
WHICH IS WRITTEN AND DESIGNED

00:45:27.930 --> 00:45:31.320
TO PROVIDE THE MUCH NEEDED AND
ENHANCED INSTRUMENT

00:45:31.320 --> 00:45:33.300
TO FUND MITIGATION EFFORTS
AGAINST

00:45:33.300 --> 00:45:34.710
THE DEVASTATING WILDFIRES

00:45:34.710 --> 00:45:36.840
THAT WE'VE SEEN IN THE STATE OF
CALIFORNIA.

00:45:37.170 --> 00:45:39.630
DURING MY 38 YEAR CAREER,

00:45:39.660 --> 00:45:42.060
OVER 38 YEARS IN THE FIRE
SERVICE,

00:45:42.060 --> 00:45:43.440
I'VE SEEN FIRSTHAND THE CHANGES

00:45:43.440 --> 00:45:45.540
IN CLIMATE AND SPECIFICALLY

00:45:45.540 --> 00:45:47.340
THE CHANGES IN FIRE BEHAVIOR
THAT

00:45:47.340 --> 00:45:48.960
HAS RESULTED IN THE LOSS OF
LIFE,

00:45:48.960 --> 00:45:51.960
HOMES AND BUSINESSES THROUGHOUT
OUR BEAUTIFUL STATE.

00:45:51.960 --> 00:45:53.790
IT'S MY HOPE THAT THIS BILL GOES
THROUGH

00:45:53.790 --> 00:45:55.620
THIS IMPORTANT PROCESS WITH
YOUR.

00:45:55.620 --> 00:45:57.930
I VOTE TO GIVE SPECIAL
DISTRICTS,

00:45:57.930 --> 00:46:00.300
COUNTIES AND CITIES WHO ARE IN
THE HIGH

00:46:00.300 --> 00:46:02.040
OR VERY HIGH SEVERITY RISK
ZONES,

00:46:02.040 --> 00:46:04.140
THE ABILITY TO FUND FIRE
HARDENED

00:46:04.140 --> 00:46:06.090
FACILITIES TO IMPROVE

00:46:06.090 --> 00:46:09.060
FIRE RESPONSE TIMES, TO KEEP
SMALL FIRES SMALL.

00:46:10.260 --> 00:46:14.040
TO PURCHASE VITALLY NEEDED
EQUIPMENT TO PROACTIVELY

00:46:14.040 --> 00:46:15.600
PERFORM VEGETATION MANAGEMENT.

00:46:15.600 --> 00:46:19.050
IN AN EXAMPLE OF THAT IS
RECENTLY WE TOOK DOWN

00:46:19.050 --> 00:46:22.410
A 20 ACRE DEAD VALENCIA GROVE
IN VALLEY CENTER,

00:46:22.530 --> 00:46:25.800
AND THEY HAD TO IMPORT THE
EQUIPMENT FROM

00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:28.710
TEXAS AND THEN RETURN IT BACK
TO TEXAS.

00:46:28.710 --> 00:46:31.020
SO WE DON'T HAVE ENOUGH
EQUIPMENT TO DO THESE.

00:46:31.020 --> 00:46:32.940
FIREBREAK AND VEGETATION
MANAGEMENT.

00:46:34.020 --> 00:46:35.940
THE DIRECT RESULT OF CLEARING
VEGETATION

00:46:35.940 --> 00:46:36.870
USING A COMBINATION

00:46:36.870 --> 00:46:39.120
OF PRESCRIBED BURNING AND BRUSH
CLEARING.

00:46:39.120 --> 00:46:41.580
USING THIS VITAL EQUIPMENT WILL
PROVIDE A MUCH

00:46:41.580 --> 00:46:44.250
NEEDED FIREBREAKS TO MITIGATE
AND PREVENT

00:46:44.250 --> 00:46:47.340
THE RAPID SPREAD OF WILDFIRE
FROM OUR WILDFIRE

00:46:47.340 --> 00:46:51.690
BACK COUNTRY TO URBAN AREAS TO
SUBURBAN AREAS,

00:46:51.690 --> 00:46:53.400
WITH THE REAL POTENTIAL OF FIRE

00:46:53.400 --> 00:46:54.989
SPREAD ALL THE WAY INTO

00:46:54.989 --> 00:46:58.950
METROPOLITAN AREAS AND THE GREAT
PACIFIC FIREBREAK.

00:46:59.640 --> 00:47:00.270
I ALSO.

00:47:00.510 --> 00:47:02.460
I ALSO HOPE THAT THE RESULTS OF
THESE EFFORTS

00:47:02.460 --> 00:47:05.430
WILL RESULT IN STABILIZING THE
INCREASE

00:47:05.430 --> 00:47:08.100
IN FIRE INSURANCE THAT OUR
RATEPAYERS ARE SEEING

00:47:08.100 --> 00:47:09.660
THROUGHOUT THE STATE OF
CALIFORNIA,

00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:12.690
GIVING HOMEOWNERS AND BUSINESSES
FINANCIAL RELIEF

00:47:12.690 --> 00:47:15.090
AND THE PEACE OF MIND KNOWING
THAT THEY

00:47:15.090 --> 00:47:17.370
ARE LIVING IN WORKING IN A FIRE
SAFE

00:47:17.370 --> 00:47:19.320
COMMUNITY THROUGH PLANNING,

00:47:19.320 --> 00:47:21.390
FUNDING AND MITIGATION.

00:47:21.420 --> 00:47:22.290
THANK YOU.

00:47:23.180 --> 00:47:23.870
YOU VERY MUCH.

00:47:23.870 --> 00:47:25.850
AND WE HAVE A SECOND LEAD
WITNESS.

00:47:26.090 --> 00:47:26.600
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU.

00:47:26.630 --> 00:47:27.260
THANK YOU, MR.

00:47:27.260 --> 00:47:27.410
CHAIR.

00:47:27.410 --> 00:47:29.330
AND MEMBERS, MARCUS DETWEILER
WITH THE CALIFORNIA

00:47:29.330 --> 00:47:31.070
SPECIAL DISTRICTS ASSOCIATION.

00:47:31.219 --> 00:47:32.390
UH, I'D LIKE TO THANK THE AUTHOR

00:47:32.390 --> 00:47:33.620
FOR BRINGING THIS IMPORTANT BILL

00:47:33.620 --> 00:47:36.410
FORWARD AND HERE TO SPEAK IN
SUPPORT,

00:47:36.410 --> 00:47:37.580
UH, PUBLIC AGENCIES,

00:47:37.580 --> 00:47:39.170
INCLUDING MUNICIPAL AND DISTRICT

00:47:39.170 --> 00:47:40.670
FIRE AGENCIES AND LOCALLY

00:47:40.670 --> 00:47:43.760
OWNED PUBLIC UTILITIES ARE
IMPORTANT STAKEHOLDERS

00:47:43.760 --> 00:47:45.350
AND PARTNERS IN THE STATE'S
FIGHT

00:47:45.350 --> 00:47:46.489
AGAINST THE DEVASTATING

00:47:46.489 --> 00:47:48.980
IMPACTS OF INCREASINGLY
HAZARDOUS WILDFIRES.

00:47:49.010 --> 00:47:51.080
AS SUCH, IT IS ENTIRELY
APPROPRIATE

00:47:51.080 --> 00:47:53.270
THAT WE ENSURE THAT THESE
AGENCIES

00:47:53.270 --> 00:47:55.400
HAVE EVERY FINANCIAL TOOL
AVAILABLE

00:47:55.400 --> 00:47:56.120
AT THEIR DISPOSAL,

00:47:56.120 --> 00:47:57.560
INCLUDING ENHANCED
INFRASTRUCTURE

00:47:57.560 --> 00:47:58.820
FINANCING DISTRICTS.

00:47:58.850 --> 00:48:01.580
THESE DISTRICTS, OR APHIDS,

00:48:01.820 --> 00:48:03.440
ARE A FORM OF TAX INCREMENT

00:48:03.440 --> 00:48:06.050
FINANCING THAT ALLOW THE
DISTRICT TO ISSUE

00:48:06.050 --> 00:48:07.610
BONDS FOR WHICH THE PROCEEDS

00:48:07.610 --> 00:48:09.320
ARE USED TO FUND SPECIFIED,

00:48:09.320 --> 00:48:12.560
UH PUBLIC FACILITIES AND PUBLIC
PROJECTS.

00:48:12.620 --> 00:48:12.739
UH.

00:48:12.739 --> 00:48:15.500
CRUCIALLY, APHIDS ARE STRUCTURED

00:48:15.500 --> 00:48:16.610
BASED ON THE VOLUNTARY

00:48:16.610 --> 00:48:19.670
PARTICIPATION OF THE AFFECTED
TAXING JURISDICTIONS.

00:48:19.670 --> 00:48:21.560
WHEREAS PREVIOUS ITERATIONS OF

00:48:21.560 --> 00:48:23.570
TAX INCREMENT FINANCING, UH,

00:48:23.570 --> 00:48:26.960
OBLIGATED TAXING JURISDICTIONS
TO FORFEIT PORTIONS

00:48:26.960 --> 00:48:29.480
OF THEIR SHARES OF PROPERTY TAX
REVENUE.

00:48:29.780 --> 00:48:32.330
UH, BY STRUCTURING IT IN THIS
WAY.

00:48:32.360 --> 00:48:35.300
UH, THIS BILL AVOIDS DIVERTING
ANY LOCAL REVENUE

00:48:35.300 --> 00:48:40.670
AND EMPOWERS AGENCIES TO UTILIZE
THIS FINANCING TOOL

00:48:40.670 --> 00:48:42.770
AND PROVIDES THEM WITH THAT
ABILITY TO

00:48:42.770 --> 00:48:44.870
FINANCE THOSE SPECIFIED
PURCHASES,

00:48:44.870 --> 00:48:47.210
THOSE FACILITIES, THOSE
PROJECTS.

00:48:47.750 --> 00:48:49.489
UM, THIS BILL SPECIFICALLY WOULD

00:48:49.489 --> 00:48:51.380
PROVIDE THAT FOR DISTRICTS

00:48:51.380 --> 00:48:55.310
LOCATED IN AT LEAST PARTIALLY IN
HIGH OR VERY HIGH,

