00:55:16.770 --> 00:55:19.050
AND THIS BILL JUST ATTEMPTS TO
CLARIFY WHAT IT MEANS

00:55:19.050 --> 00:55:21.420
TO ATTRIBUTE THE COST OF SERVICE
TO A PARCEL,

00:55:21.420 --> 00:55:23.280
AND TO BUILD ON WHY THIS IS
IMPORTANT

00:55:23.280 --> 00:55:24.510
FOR PUBLIC UTILITIES.

00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:26.820
WATER RATE DESIGN CAN TAKE MANY
SHAPES AND IS

00:55:26.820 --> 00:55:29.070
AN IMPORTANT CONSERVATION AND
EQUITY TOOL.

00:55:29.070 --> 00:55:30.390
UNIFORM RATES, FOR EXAMPLE,

00:55:30.390 --> 00:55:32.520
ARE LIKE GAS PRICES YOU JUST PAY
PER GALLON.

00:55:32.580 --> 00:55:34.170
UH, TIERED RATES, BY COMPARISON,

00:55:34.170 --> 00:55:35.040
INCREASE THE PRICE PER

00:55:35.040 --> 00:55:37.650
GALLON WHEN YOU ENTER SPECIFIC
TIERS OF WATER USE.

00:55:37.650 --> 00:55:39.239
IN BOTH INSTANCES, YOU PAY MORE

00:55:39.239 --> 00:55:40.260
FOR THE WATER YOU USE.

00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:41.460
BUT TIERED RATES HAVE THE ADDED

00:55:41.460 --> 00:55:42.719
BENEFIT OF SENDING A CLEAR

00:55:42.719 --> 00:55:45.060
SIGNAL TO CUSTOMERS THAT ABOVE
A CERTAIN THRESHOLD,

00:55:45.060 --> 00:55:47.070
WATER IS GOING TO GET MORE
EXPENSIVE.

00:55:47.070 --> 00:55:48.989
RATE STRUCTURES, WHEN DESIGNED
CORRECTLY,

00:55:48.989 --> 00:55:51.540
NOT ONLY INCENTIVIZE
CONSERVATION AND EFFICIENCY,

00:55:51.540 --> 00:55:53.580
BUT THEY ALSO HELP TO ALLOCATE
THE INCREMENTAL

00:55:53.580 --> 00:55:55.890
COSTS OF HIGHER WATER USE ON
THOSE CUSTOMERS

00:55:55.890 --> 00:55:58.050
THAT DRIVE THE NEED FOR A SYSTEM
CAPABLE

00:55:58.050 --> 00:55:59.580
OF MEETING THAT HIGHER WATER
USE.

00:55:59.580 --> 00:56:00.270
IN OTHER WORDS.

00:56:00.440 --> 00:56:02.330
THEY ASSIGNED TWO PARCELS THE
PROPORTIONAL COST OF

00:56:02.330 --> 00:56:05.780
SERVICE ATTRIBUTABLE TO THAT
PARCEL UNDER PROP 22.

00:56:05.900 --> 00:56:07.010
PROPORTIONALITY REQUIREMENTS.

00:56:07.010 --> 00:56:08.810
THE PERFECT COMPLIANCE SCENARIO
WOULD BE TO

00:56:08.810 --> 00:56:11.000
TRACK EVERY INDIVIDUAL WATER
MOLECULE,

00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:12.620
AND EXACTLY WHEN THOSE MOLECULES

00:56:12.620 --> 00:56:14.060
ARE USED TO PERFECTLY MAP

00:56:14.060 --> 00:56:15.830
OUT THE EXACT COSTS EACH PARCEL

00:56:15.830 --> 00:56:16.880
PLACES ON THE SYSTEM,

00:56:16.880 --> 00:56:19.250
AND THAT IS AN IMPOSSIBLE
STANDARD.

00:56:19.520 --> 00:56:21.350
ACCORDINGLY, CALIFORNIA COURTS
HAVE REPEATEDLY

00:56:21.350 --> 00:56:24.260
SAID THAT PROP 18 DOES NOT
REQUIRE PERFECTION,

00:56:24.260 --> 00:56:26.030
AND THERE'S AN UNDERSTANDING
THAT THE METHODS

00:56:26.030 --> 00:56:27.650
THAT REASONABLY ASSESS THE COST
OF

00:56:27.650 --> 00:56:29.989
SERVICE ATTRIBUTABLE TO A PARCEL
COMPLY

00:56:29.989 --> 00:56:31.700
WITH THIS PROPORTIONALITY
REQUIREMENT.

00:56:31.700 --> 00:56:33.830
BUT AS WE'VE SAID,

00:56:33.830 --> 00:56:34.880
WHAT WE'VE SEEN IS THAT COURTS
HAVE

00:56:34.880 --> 00:56:36.920
LEANED MORE INTO THE PERFECT
SCENARIO REQUIREMENTS,

00:56:36.920 --> 00:56:38.510
WHERE RATE STRUCTURES HAVE TO
BE JUSTIFIED

00:56:38.510 --> 00:56:39.860
BASED ON SPECIFIC TIME OF USE,

00:56:39.860 --> 00:56:41.989
METERING AND MOLECULE BY
MOLECULE DATA.

00:56:42.020 --> 00:56:43.489
ELSE THEY VIOLATE PROP 18.

00:56:43.489 --> 00:56:45.890
AND THIS BILL JUST TRIES TO
CLARIFY THAT PROP 218

00:56:45.950 --> 00:56:48.140
PROPORTIONALITY REQUIREMENT IS
NOT SO STRINGENT,

00:56:48.140 --> 00:56:49.219
AND THAT WATER SUPPLIERS MAY

00:56:49.219 --> 00:56:50.600
USE METHODS THAT REASONABLY,

00:56:50.600 --> 00:56:52.460
NOT PERFECTLY ASSESS THE COST OF

00:56:52.460 --> 00:56:53.930
SERVICE ATTRIBUTED TO A PARCEL.

