01:24:04.790 --> 01:24:06.320
EMPLOYEE HOUSING PROJECTS.

01:24:06.320 --> 01:24:08.510
THE PROJECTS PROPOSED PURSUANT
TO THAT BILL

01:24:08.510 --> 01:24:10.550
ARE REQUIRED TO MEET NUMEROUS
CRITERIA,

01:24:10.550 --> 01:24:11.810
INCLUDING THAT THEY MUST BE

01:24:11.810 --> 01:24:13.400
LOCATED ON LANDS DESIGNATED

01:24:13.400 --> 01:24:15.680
FOR AGRICULTURE AND THE GENERAL
PLAN,

01:24:15.680 --> 01:24:17.060
AND THAT PROJECTS MUST INCLUDE

01:24:17.060 --> 01:24:18.920
NO MORE THAN 36 UNITS.

01:24:18.920 --> 01:24:21.320
UNFORTUNATELY, THESE LIMITATIONS

01:24:21.320 --> 01:24:22.850
MEAN THAT THERE ARE FEW PROJECTS

01:24:22.850 --> 01:24:24.470
THAT COULD POTENTIALLY QUALIFY
FOR

01:24:24.470 --> 01:24:26.270
STREAMLINING IN MY DISTRICT.

01:24:26.270 --> 01:24:28.550
IN PARTICULAR, MOST SITES IN MY
DISTRICT THAT

01:24:28.550 --> 01:24:31.010
COULD POTENTIALLY QUALIFY ARE
OUTSIDE OF

01:24:31.010 --> 01:24:33.500
CITIES AND OTHER URBANIZED AREAS
AND LACK

01:24:33.530 --> 01:24:36.110
THE NEEDED WATER AND SEWER
INFRASTRUCTURE.

01:24:36.110 --> 01:24:40.400
SO WE ARE HERE WITH AB 3035 TO
MAKES TWO CHANGES

01:24:40.400 --> 01:24:42.740
TO BROADEN THE SITES WHERE
AGRICULTURAL

01:24:42.740 --> 01:24:45.110
EMPLOYEE HOUSING CAN BE
STREAMLINED IN

01:24:45.110 --> 01:24:47.270
SANTA CLARA AND SANTA CRUZ
COUNTIES.

01:24:47.270 --> 01:24:49.820
FIRST, IT EXPANDS THE SITE
QUALIFICATION TO

01:24:49.820 --> 01:24:52.400
INCLUDE AREAS NEAR AGRICULTURAL
LAND THAT

01:24:52.400 --> 01:24:54.770
ARE MORE LIKELY TO HAVE WATER
AND SEWER SERVICE

01:24:54.770 --> 01:24:57.290
THAT CAN SUPPORT MULTI-UNIT
HOUSING.

01:24:57.320 --> 01:24:59.210
SECOND, IT INCREASES THE NUMBER

01:24:59.210 --> 01:25:00.650
OF UNITS THAT CAN BE INCLUDED

01:25:00.650 --> 01:25:04.070
IN A QUALIFYING DEVELOPMENT TO
REFLECT THE ECONOMIES

01:25:04.070 --> 01:25:05.750
OF SCALE TYPICALLY REQUIRED TO

01:25:05.750 --> 01:25:07.580
DEVELOP HOUSING AND EXPENSIVE

01:25:07.580 --> 01:25:10.250
HOUSING MARKETS LIKE THOSE IN
MY DISTRICT.

01:25:10.250 --> 01:25:12.830
WHILE AB 3035 IS A DISTRICT
BILL,

01:25:12.830 --> 01:25:14.270
WE HOPE THAT THIS PILOT PROJECT

01:25:14.270 --> 01:25:15.620
CAN HELP INFORM FUTURE

01:25:15.620 --> 01:25:18.350
OPPORTUNITIES TO STREAMLINE THIS
MUCH NEEDED

01:25:18.350 --> 01:25:20.660
HOUSING FOR FARM WORKERS
STATEWIDE.

01:25:20.660 --> 01:25:22.550
AND WITH ME TO TESTIFY IN
SUPPORT

01:25:22.550 --> 01:25:24.050
TODAY IS DAVID CAMPOS,

01:25:24.080 --> 01:25:26.090
THE DEPUTY COUNTY EXECUTIVE FOR

01:25:26.090 --> 01:25:27.560
THE COUNTY OF SANTA CLARA.

01:25:28.910 --> 01:25:30.500
&GT;&GT; THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

01:25:30.590 --> 01:25:32.540
UH, ASSEMBLY MEMBER PELLERIN.

01:25:32.540 --> 01:25:35.960
MADAM CHAIR, HONOURABLE MEMBERS,
UH, DAVID CAMPOS,

01:25:35.960 --> 01:25:37.400
DEPUTY COUNTY EXECUTIVE FOR

01:25:37.400 --> 01:25:39.020
THE COUNTY OF SANTA CLARA.

01:25:39.020 --> 01:25:40.250
ON BEHALF OF THE COUNTY,

01:25:40.250 --> 01:25:42.140
I'M HERE TO SIMPLY ASK YOU TO
GIVE

01:25:42.140 --> 01:25:44.180
US THIS TOOL SO THAT WE CAN DO

01:25:44.180 --> 01:25:46.820
BETTER BY OUR FARM WORKERS.

01:25:46.850 --> 01:25:50.630
THE FACT IS THAT WE AS A COUNTY,
WE AS A STATE,

01:25:50.630 --> 01:25:52.670
MUST DO BETTER FOR THE PEOPLE

01:25:52.670 --> 01:25:54.470
THAT PUT FOOD ON THE TABLE,

01:25:54.470 --> 01:25:56.000
AND WHEN YOU HAVE BEFORE YOU

01:25:56.000 --> 01:25:57.590
IS A PRETTY MODEST BILL THAT

01:25:57.590 --> 01:26:00.770
ESSENTIALLY BUILDS ON THE WORK
THAT SPEAKER RIVAS

01:26:00.770 --> 01:26:03.350
